// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 13 „Keskkond ja vastutustundlik elu” (b1b2-061…065), stage B2.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, the cast a year after the B1 course
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): on Viktor's farm in Kõrvemaa the winters have become mild, the well runs dry in August and the
// spruce woods turn grey; now the energy firm Rohevool (developer Mart Lõhmus) plans a nine-turbine wind farm on the old
// peat field 2.5 km from his village (village elder Leida Saarik, neighbour Aivar Mänd, planning head Tarmo Kangur,
// bird scientist Kertu Allik). At Tuul Logistika Sofia makes the firm's first environmental overview for a Swedish client
// (72 % of the footprint from vans and lorries) and with Markus and Liis compares electric vans, route planning with
// artificial intelligence, cargo bikes and eco-driving training; the board gives 60 000 euros. Jaan runs the zero-waste
// week at Kase kool (40 kg of food thrown away a day). One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner takes
// part in the public hearing on the wind farm in Kõrvemaa village hall (debate with pro / contra cards → a joint
// proposal) and writes an argumentative opinion text of 180–200 words for the parish paper (064 Kasuta).
// Grammar (B2 spiral, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): change of state + translative (muutuma / jääma / minema + -ks,
// -nema verbs: kliima muutub soojemaks, kaev jääb kuivaks) taught in 061 (notice, rule table, word forms, transformation,
// used in the Kasuta overview), back in 063 (muutub lühemaks / väiksemaks) and 064; cause and effect connectors with word
// order and the impersonal and the quotative in environmental news (esitati, tellitakse; olevat, muutuvat; X-i sõnul,
// väidetavalt) taught in 062, back in 064 (the hearing); nominalisation -mine with comparison (heitmete vähendamine,
// 22 000 euro võrra kallim) in 063, back in 064; concessive kuigi / siiski / küll…, kuid / vaatamata and the problem →
// causes → solutions → conclusion text in 064.
// Harno B2 formats: 4-option cloze (061), long article with multiple choice (062), interview → gaps and true / false
// (063), sentence bank and lecture notes (064), debate with pro / contra cards and a decision (063, 064 Kasuta), letters
// of 140–200 words. Module 12's words return: andmed, rakendus, kasutaja, tehisintellekt, turvalisus, ekraaniaeg,
// teavitus, valeinfo, allikas, usaldusväärne, pealkiri, postitus, fakt, autor, kahtlema, jagama, kontrollima, link,
// koolitus, vastutus, oht, otsus, oskus, asendama, privaatsus, petukõne.
//   061 Viktor's article in the parish paper (four problems as one chain), a cloze on farms and a warmer climate, a radio
//       interview with climate scientist Peeter Uibo; Sofia and Markus write Tuul Logistika's first overview.
//   062 radio news on the wind farm, an article on wind turbines and false information; a scare post in the village
//       group, Sofia's call with Viktor and his calm reply with sources.
//   063 four solution cards, an interview with fleet manager Ott Kuusik (electric vans in winter), Markus's proposal;
//       Liis's voice message and the 60 000-euro budget choice for the board.
//   064 Jaan's school-paper article on food waste, a zero-waste article (sentence bank), Merit Rebane's opening lecture;
//       the public hearing and the opinion text.
// Final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 13): 061 AVAS R→S, 062 LUGU R→W, 063 PROB L→S, 064 KUUL L→W,
// 065 EKS. Exam corners (one Harno B2 task a teaching lesson): 061 R1 (Viktor's article, predict and check), 062 W2a
// (summary of the village survey chart + own comment), 063 L4 (Ott Kuusik's interview, 12 true / false), 064 L1 (ten
// short announcements, played once). Main Kasuta tasks: 061 S16 overview at the team meeting (recorded at home), 062 W13
// reply in the village group, 063 S17 budget debate with argument cards, 064 W14 opinion text for the parish paper.
// The exam 065 has four timed parts (PART): L3 + L2, R1 + R4, W1 + W2b, S1 + S2.
// Lesson 5 (065) is the module's check in Harno B2 form. The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module13.js.
